> Other than what makes you think it's a low percentage play?

The part of the game where serial ascenders do die is the early game.
The PR provides an advantage mainly in the middle game (it makes the
early game before you get to minetown harder, makes midgame a bit
easier with a big AC buffer and doesn't matter in the late game
because you'll have enough protection then anyway). Serial ascenders
can handle the midgame fine. They don't need the AC buffer the
protection run provides.

The protection run makes the early game harder in exchange for making
the midgame easier. Good players very rarely die in the mid or late
game if they're playing to maximise ascensions. So, it's a bad trade
off for them.

If you find yourself able to complete the PR but not cope with the
midgame then your midgame play is poor. You'd do better to improve
your midgame play than to focus on the PR as a way to get an extra AC
buffer.

